Pair /: Pair::usage = "Pair[x, y] is the head of a special pairing used in \
the internal\nrepresentation: x and y may have heads LorentzIndex or \
Momentum.\n\nIf both x and y have head LorentzIndex, the metric tensor (e.g. \
$g^{\\mu \\nu}$)\nis understood.\n\nIf x and y have head Momentum, a scalar \
product (e.g. $p \\cdot q$) is meant.\n\nIf one of x and y has head \
LorentzIndex and the other Momentum, a Lorentz\nvector (e.g. $p^{\\mu }$) is \
implied."
 
