FCChargeConjugateTransposed /: FCChargeConjugateTransposed::usage = "FCCharge\
ConjugateTransposed[exp] represents the application of the \
charge\nconjugation operator to the transposed of exp, i.e. $C^{-1} \
\\text{exp}^T C$.\nHere exp is understood to be a single Dirac matrix or a \
chain thereof. The\noption setting Explicit determines whether the explicit \
result is returned or\nwhether it is left in the unevaluated form.The \
unevaluated form will be also\nmaintained if the function does not know how \
to obtain $C^{-1} \\text{exp}^T C$\nfrom the given exp.\n\nThe shortcut for \
FCChargeConjugateTransposed is FCCCT."
 
NonCommFreeQ[Pair[LorentzIndex[\[Mu], D], LorentzIndex[\[Nu], D]]] = True
 
NonCommFreeQ[Pair[LorentzIndex[\[Mu], D], Momentum[2*k1 + k2 + 2*k3 - 2*l, 
        D]]*Pair[LorentzIndex[\[Nu], D], Momentum[2*k1 + k3 - 2*l, D]]] = True
 
