FCLoopCreateRuleGLIToGLI /: FCLoopCreateRuleGLIToGLI::usage = "FCLoopCreateRu\
leGLIToGLI[topology1, topology2] creates a GLI replacement rule\nassuming \
that the topology2 is a subtopology of topology1. Both topologies\nmust be \
given as FCTopology objects.\n\nIt is also possible to use \
FCLoopCreateRuleGLIToGLI[topo1, {subtopo1,\nsubtopo2, ...}] provided that \
{subtopo1, subtopo2, ...} are subtopologies of\ntopo1 that were obtained by \
removing some propagators from topo1 and not\nperforming any loop momentum \
shifts afterwards.\n\nFurthermore, when working with lists of topologies one \
can write\nFCLoopCreateRuleGLIToGLI[{topo1, topo2, ...}, {{subtopo11, \
subtopo12, ...},\n{subtopo21, subtopo22, ...}, ..}]."
 
